text:
🚨NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman says the U.S. would struggle to maintain space dominance over China without SpaceX.

“We can't send astronauts to and from the space station without them. We can't have down mass of our science experiments from the space station without them. The Nancy Grace Roman telescope that's going out to pursue the secrets of the universe was launched on a Falcon Heavy not that long ago.”

In 2025, SpaceX delivered more than 80% of the world’s total mass to orbit.

SpaceX’s Crew Dragon is currently NASA’s only certified American spacecraft routinely carrying astronauts, scientific research, and hardware to and from the ISS.

On August 30, SpaceX’s Falcon Heavy launched NASA’s $4 billion-class Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope toward L2, roughly one million miles from Earth.

Isaacman: “The United States would be seriously challenged in the high ground of space without their capabilities.”

